      "reasoning": "NBRC 1116, 1195, 1196 and 1200 and TOGO M2186, M2708 and M3181 explicitly use volume-dosed concentrated HCl reagent. This record denotes the qualitative source-described acid preparation, with variable or unspecified strength, not pure gaseous HCl or a certified commercial formulation. It preserves the source reagent boundary at UNDEFINED_MIXTURE granularity. NBRC 1200 prints 51.3 mL where NBRC 1195/1196 print 51.3 microlitres; these receiving-stock quantities remain unresolved and are not used to derive acid strength. No percentage, molarity, aqueous solvent, supplier, grade, excipients or exact equivalence between source lots is established. This bounded qualitative preparation supports source association only; quantitative stock reconstruction and equivalence to a specified acid product remain unapproved. Successor-v3: Literal 25%, 32% and 35% are retained as source specifications, not normalized comparable fractions. The cited sources do not state a common percentage basis, carrier, grade or assay tolerance; the exact same-or-distinct preparation relation is unresolved. TOGO M2305/M2746 explicitly calls its 25% input concentrated, so that qualitative label does not exclude a numerical percentage. If comparable definitions and assay ranges were established, a real strength difference could be assessed; they are not established here. Before co-installing overlapping candidates, the coordinator must choose an explicit common bounded partial-material scope preserving every source context, or obtain comparable preparation/product evidence. No owner merge or arbitrary winner is selected.",
      "applicability": "All 1 full frozen occurrence snapshots and linked captured primary contexts were independently reread for case 125. NBRC 1116, 1195, 1196 and 1200 and TOGO M2186, M2708 and M3181 explicitly use volume-dosed concentrated HCl reagent. This record denotes the qualitative source-described acid preparation, with variable or unspecified strength, not pure gaseous HCl or a certified commercial formulation. It preserves the source reagent boundary at UNDEFINED_MIXTURE granularity. NBRC 1200 prints 51.3 mL where NBRC 1195/1196 print 51.3 microlitres; these receiving-stock quantities remain unresolved and are not used to derive acid strength. This association is source-bound; raw generic labels remain nonresolving provenance unless explicitly the spelling-only seawater alias. Existing source occurrences only; W02 M2305/M2746 is comparative evidence and does not add its cases or occurrences to this proposal.",
      "missing_requirement": "Bounded named preparation remains supportable. Comparable percentage/product evidence or an explicit common partial-material convention is required before overlap reconciliation/co-installation; not a prerequisite for recording the literal source input."
    },
    {
      "source_index": 178,
      "case_id": "KG_CASE:d46699260f46a04bc704500d3c6d4e42c066e851c05cec51d6e4d25a1a899905",
      "reasoning": "JCM1270 identifies the44g BD-Difco dry base before separate950mL water and50mL sheep blood. The actual manufacturer-authored BD2009 second-edition PDF, captured from NMSU, printedp158/PDFpage170, verifies the seven nominal Difco constituents and separately distinguishes BBL andEH. This replaces the original web-search wrapper as primary support. The approximate formula and performance-adjustment footnote do not prove a historical lot. Retain PARTIAL names-only components and no dry mass-ratio inference. Direct JCM sheep blood differs from MediaDive steps naming horse blood; MediaDive table gives100mLsheep/900mLwater. These receiving-medium discrepancies do not add blood or water to the dry base.",
      "applicability": "Only frozen mediadive.ingredient:2046 BD-Difco44g row associated with JCM1270. Nominal2009 manufacturer formulation is supporting product context, not a historical-lot certificate. Existing mixed generic Columbia owner continuity remains coordinator work; no new broad source routes or alternate-product equivalence.",
      "missing_requirement": "No missing fact blocks the bounded manual-evidence correction. Historical lot details and existing mixed-owner continuity/admission remain separate limitations."
    }
  ],
